    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0124" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/2–2548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-25">February 25,
                        1948</date>.<lb/>[Received February 26—6:14 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. ReContel 86, 20th.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d87-f1"/> Communist North Shensi
                    radio February 11 reported that capture Liaoyang was effected within matter of
                    hours after launching of general attack on morning of 16th, fighting having been
                    brought to conclusion by afternoon same day. Same radio February 16 reported
                    Communists took 10,700 plus prisoners at time capture of city.</p>
                <p>Same radio February 24 reported destruction at Anshan of 25th Division of
                    Nationalist Fifty-second Army and Communications Police Column with total
                    Nationalist casualties including prisoners 12,997 upon capture of town on 19th.
                    Prisoners at Anshan by same report totaled 10,558 troops.</p>
                <p>Latter radio report stated further that Nationalist temporary 62d Division was
                    destroyed on 19th between Faku and Ch’ang-t’u, total casualties that division
                    given as 7,238 men including over 6,000 prisoners.</p>
                <p>Sent Department as 95, repeated Nanking as 150, Tientsin and Mukden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
